{"go_to_market_strategy": {"title": "Go-to-Market Strategy", "content": "The initial go-to-market strategy will focus on directly engaging MBA students through digital channels, academic forums, and student networks within the United States. This approach aims to highlight the benefits of personalized learning support and efficiency that the AI tutor could offer, leveraging students' general familiarity with AI tools like ChatGPT (this familiarity is an assumption). Direct engagement is intended to bypass potential institutional adoption hurdles, though specific MBA student engagement channels and preferences are currently unconfirmed.

Addressing the reported relatively low perception of AI benefits in education among the US public (some reports suggest only 39% consider it beneficial) and the adoption gap among higher education faculty (with some data indicating only 22% regularly use generative AI compared to 83% of K-12 teachers) will be critical. This requires developing clear communication strategies and product demonstrations that emphasize academic integrity, human oversight, and the tutor's role as a supplementary tool, not a replacement for faculty. The effectiveness of this trust-building strategy is hypothetical.

